  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Evaluate the double integral ${\u222c}_{R}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x\\text{\u00a0}{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}A$ over the rectangle $R=[0,\\pi ]\\times [0,1].$",
  "worked_solution": "We apply the multiplicative property of double integrals and then evaluate each of the integrals separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\u222c}_{R}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x\\text{\u00a0}{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\u222c}_{R}(\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x)\\text{\u00a0}({e}^{y})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =({\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =[-\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x]_{0}^{\\pi }\\cdot [{e}^{y}]_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =-(\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\pi -\\operatorname{cos}\u20610)\\cdot ({e}^{1}-{e}^{0}) \\\\  & =-(-1-1)\\cdot (e-1) \\\\  & =2(e-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
